  "id": "lateral-geniculate-nucleus",
  "term": "lateral geniculate nucleus",
  "definition": "The lateral geniculate nucleus is a part of the thalamus in the visual system that receives input from the retina and passes visual signals on toward primary visual cortex. Rather than acting as a purely passive relay, it helps filter and shape visual information early in the visual pathway.",
